From 8e6235f67d6d7351ad2fe4b097d6d73b25c9b67c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris <16943149+nepenth@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 16:42:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 24/24] [Build] Limit FlashAttention submodules for CUDA builds

The vllm-flash-attn repository also declares ROCm AITER and Composable Kernel
submodules. FetchContent's default recursive submodule update downloads both
trees during a CUDA-only build, including AITER's nested ROCm dependencies.

Only CUTLASS is required by the CUDA extension. Restrict the checkout to that
submodule so ARM64 source builds do not spend substantial time and disk space
retrieving unused ROCm sources.
---
 cmake/external_projects/vllm_flash_attn.cmake | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/cmake/external_projects/vllm_flash_attn.cmake b/cmake/external_projects/vllm_flash_attn.cmake
index d11eaa537..6c3b94693 100644
--- a/cmake/external_projects/vllm_flash_attn.cmake
+++ b/cmake/external_projects/vllm_flash_attn.cmake
@@ -40,6 +40,7 @@ else()
           vllm-flash-attn
           GIT_REPOSITORY https://github.com/vllm-project/flash-attention.git
           GIT_TAG 28e862d21806bc3580207aa0ad4e2759151e9827
+          GIT_SUBMODULES csrc/cutlass
           GIT_PROGRESS TRUE
           # Don't share the vllm-flash-attn build between build types
           BINARY_DIR ${CMAKE_BINARY_DIR}/vllm-flash-attn
-- 
